  "style": {
    "name": "medieval defensive gatehouse",
    "rationale": "A near-monochrome stone keep pierced by one arched passage: stone_bricks body, cobblestone plinth/string-course/corner buttresses and roof verge, deepslate_tiles steep gable roof reading as silhouette, and a single warm dark_oak_log voussoir gate front and back. Footprint 28W x 20D, walls to y29, gable ridge running front-to-back so the triangle faces the entry and frames the arch; ratio ~1.5:1 tall-to-wide for a defensive guard-block. Modelled in the round — four enclosing walls, two arched gates, two slit windows per side, and a finished four-sloped... gable roof with the hidden back mirrored from the single-view concept."
  },
